                                "sense_id": "ecf412ae-d0a9-3a90-834c-2cf0fb6e7d95",
                                "text": "It must always be remembered that although to an adult a particular belief may seem like a coelacanthine survival from the past, to the schoolchild who learns it from his mate the belief is a novelty; it is something just learnt, and often excitingly full of possibility for his immediate welfare."
